  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "Detroit techno: a minor-ninth chord stab struck on a syncopated pattern over the four, sixteenth hats, a clap on two and four — the soulful, string-and-keys side of techno",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars of stabs: struck on one, the a of one, three-and, then two-and and four in the second bar, voiced as a stacked ninth on a warm electric keyboard that rings a little. Sixteenth hats with the offbeat lifted. The strings that often double the stabs are the composer's own pad."
  }
